; Stage 15 W4c (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md §W4c), the "related
; shape worth a dedicated diagnostic": an extra `)` inside a multi-binding `let`
; ends the binding list early and silently turns the next binding into a body
; statement. Note this leaves the binding list at an EVEN element count
; (`(a:i32 1)` -- two elements), so the pre-existing "binding list must be even"
; check cannot see it; and when the user compensates with one fewer `)` at the
; end (as here) the file still balances, so the reader cannot see it either.
; Before: `undefined: b:i32` -- correct location, but it names the symptom.
; After:  the message names the cause, at the `let`'s own line.
(defn main ():i32
  (let (a:i32 1)
        b:i32 2)
    (return (+ a b)))
